From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:34:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v2] ath11k: convert station vdev 802.11 frames for the NSS firmware

Frames mac80211 sends as 802.11, which include every EAPOL frame, are
converted to ethernet before they go to the NSS firmware. The conversion
takes the receiver's interface type and is always given a station's, and
ieee80211_data_to_8023() rejects a ToDS frame for a station. On a
station vdev every such frame is dropped and the 4-way handshake never
completes. Pass an access point's interface type for a station vdev.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5

Keep AP and station frame conversion in the shared integer-return TX
path while NSS owns data transmission.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -6658,11 +6658,12 @@ static int ath11k_mac_tx(struct ieee8021
 	 * The conversion is the subsystem's own, and it is written for the
 	 * receiving side: it refuses a frame travelling away from the
 	 * distribution system on an access point, which is every frame an
-	 * access point sends. A frame leaving here is bit for bit the frame a
-	 * station receives, so it is converted as that station would - the
-	 * address it is told to expect is the frame's own first address,
-	 * which is what makes the check it performs vacuous rather than
-	 * wrong.
+	 * access point sends. A frame leaving here is bit for bit the frame
+	 * its receiver gets, so it is converted as the receiver would: as a
+	 * station for an access point's frame, as an access point for a
+	 * station's - the address it is told to expect is the frame's own
+	 * first address, which is what makes the check it performs vacuous
+	 * rather than wrong.
 	 */
 	/* A mesh device carries 802.11, without the QoS control the
 	 * hardware inserts itself.
@@ -6689,6 +6690,8 @@ static int ath11k_mac_tx(struct ieee8021
 
 		if (!(info_flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_HW_80211_ENCAP) &&
 		    ieee80211_data_to_8023(skb, hdr->addr1,
+					   vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION ?
+					   NL80211_IFTYPE_AP :
 					   NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION)) {
 			ieee80211_free_txskb(ar->hw, skb);
 			return 0;
